# tin-orchestra.trk -- "Tin Orchestra". A gamelan-shaped piece in a pelog-
# like five-note set (C Db Eb G Ab = 1 2 3 5 6), 16 rows per bar, 56 bars,
# tempo moving 76 -> 108 -> 60 BPM (the form drives the transport).
# Levels and tempo in tin-orchestra-form.trk; the patterns below the line
# are generated from the two balungan by tools in the album's thread and
# then edited by hand.
#
# Layers, as in a gamelan: the gong closes every four bars, the kenong
# marks each bar's last beat, the saron plays the balungan (one note a
# beat), and two Surge modal resonators interlock the kotekan in 16ths:
# polos on the even rows, sangsih on the odd. Every bonang note locks its
# own material (cva), so no two strokes ring the same.
#
#   balungan a: 2 1 2 6 | 3 5 3 2 | 5 6 5 3 | 2 1 2 6
#   balungan b: 3 3 6 5 | 6 5 3 2 | 5 3 2 1 | 3 2 1 6

track saron   note vel cva              # 1  native modal bars: cva = structure
track kenong  note vel cva              # 2  Surge Twist 2-op FM: cva = FM amount
track gong    note vel                  # 3  native FM gong
track polos   note vel cva              # 4  Surge Twist Modal Resonator: cva = material
track sangsih note vel cva              # 5  Surge Twist Modal Resonator: cva = material
track kick    note vel                  # 6  native kick
track shk     note vel                  # 7  native shaker, 7-row loop

pattern kick 4x16 kick
1:00 | x .6
1:10 | x?.5 .35
2:00 | x .55
2:08 | x .4
3:00 | x .6
3:10 | x?.5 .35
4:00 | x .55
4:06 | x?.5 .3
4:12 | x .65

pattern shk7 7 shk
00 | x .5
02 | x?.6 .3
04 | x@.2 .35
05 | x?.5 .25

